  "ingredients": [
    "6 ounce breakfast sausage",
    "4 large egg",
    "4 tablespoon unsweetened carton coconut milk",
    "4 tablespoon low-carb maple syrup",
    "1 teaspoon vanilla extract",
    "20 drop liquid stevia",
    "1 1/2 cup almond flour",
    "1 teaspoon baking powder",
    "1/4 cup erythritol",
    "2 tablespoon psyllium husk powder",
    "1/4 teaspoon salt"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "If using Jimmy Dean sausage, just cut the log in half and go ahead and get started. If not, measure out the sausage and break it up into small pieces.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/maple-sausage-pancake-muffins/#wprm-recipe-51217-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_8756.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Turn a pan up to high heat and fry the outsides of the sausage until crisp. The insides will continue to cook during the baking process.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/maple-sausage-pancake-muffins/#wprm-recipe-51217-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_8758.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 350F. Add the eggs, coconut milk, maple syrup, vanilla extract, and liquid stevia in a mixing bowl.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/maple-sausage-pancake-muffins/#wprm-recipe-51217-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_8769.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine well, ensuring that all of the ingredients are evenly distributed.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/maple-sausage-pancake-muffins/#wprm-recipe-51217-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_8773.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a separate bowl, measure out the almond flour, baking powder, erythritol, psyllium husk powder, and salt.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/maple-sausage-pancake-muffins/#wprm-recipe-51217-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_8777.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix the wet and dry ingredients, then add all of the seared sausage pieces to the mixture.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/maple-sausage-pancake-muffins/#wprm-recipe-51217-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_8787.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Divide the batter into silicone cupcake molds and bake for 20–25 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/maple-sausage-pancake-muffins/#wprm-recipe-51217-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_87932.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once cooked, remove from the oven and let cool for 5 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/maple-sausage-pancake-muffins/#wprm-recipe-51217-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_8798.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Remove from the silicone cupcake molds and place on a cooling rack, if storing in the fridge. Otherwise, serve warm.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/maple-sausage-pancake-muffins/#wprm-recipe-51217-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/07/IMG_8807.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/maple-sausage-pancake-muffins/#wprm-recipe-51217-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
