    "video": {
      "name": "Keto Recipe - Maple Sausage Pancake Muffins",
      "description": "These little keto muffins are packed full of deliciousness – sausage, maple syrup, and a sweet pancake-ish fluffy muffin to encase all of the flavor. They are an awesome way to pre-cook your breakfast in the morning. If you’re the type of person that rushes out the door and likes to bring breakfast with you to work – then give these a try!\n\nIf you’re a bulk cooker, feel free to freeze them too – they work well in the freezer. Just make sure you wrap them up in plastic wrap and then into a plastic container.\n\nRead the full recipe with full nutrition breakdown and step-by-step pictures over at:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nIngredients:\n6 ounces ground sausage\n1 ½ cups almond flour\n4 large eggs\n4 tablespoons coconut milk\n4 tablespoons Ruled.me maple syrup (or any sugar-free maple syrup)\n2 tablespoons psyllium husk powder\n1 teaspoon vanilla extract\n1 teaspoon baking powder\n¼ teaspoon salt\n20 drops liquid Stevia\n¼ cup erythritol\n\nNutrition Summary:\nThis will make a total of 12 Maple Sausage Pancake Muffins. Each muffin comes out to 160.5 Calories, 12.88g Fats, 2.16g Net Carbs, and 7.6g Protein.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSee more keto recipes, knowledge and tips on the website to keep your weight loss going strong.\n\nEverything you need to know about the keto diet:\n\nGetting started? Everything you need is here:\n\nWe also make things easy with this 30 day diet plan:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFollow Ruled.Me for more tasty food:",
